 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $87.0B in FY2026 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +3.3% over FY2017..FY2026 [2].\nNet income was $16.0B in FY2026 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2026 was +3.3% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2026 was +0.5% [3] [5].\nIn FY2026, net income growth of +0.5% [3] [5] was below revenue growth of +3.3% [1] [4].\nIn FY2026, operating cash flow growth of +9.8% [6] [7] was above net income growth of +0.5% [3] [5].\n\n## Margins\nOperating margin was 22.7% in FY2026 [8].\nOperating margin changed -1.6pp in FY2026 [8] [9].\nNet margin was 18.4% in FY2026 [10].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2026, free cash flow of $15.1B [11] was below net income of $16.0B [3].\nThe current ratio was 0.68\u00d7 in FY2026 [12], below 1.00\u00d7.\nIn FY2026, operating cash flow of $19.6B [6] was above net income of $16.0B [3].\n\n## Red flags\nCurrent ratio is below 1.0 (0.68\u00d7 in FY2026). Source operands: Current ratio 0.8770x in FY2017 [13]; Current ratio 0.6773x in FY2026 [12].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from +3.3% in FY2026 [1] [4].\nWatch how operating margin in the next reporting update compares with 22.7% in FY2026 [8].\nWatch how free cash flow in the next reporting update compares with $15.1B in FY2026 [11].",
